  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dutch expertise on hydrogen &amp; critical raw materials at EU-GCC Events in Riyadh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity supports the participation of two Dutch experts, one on hydrogen and one on critical raw materials, in the EU-GCC Green Transition Forum in Riyadh on 6 October 2025. The event brings together European and Gulf stakeholders to discuss cooperation on key energy transition topics, including hydrogen, critical raw materials and carbon capture and storage.The participation highlights Dutch expertise in clean hydrogen and related value chains, while strengthening dialogue with Gulf partners. It also contributes to preparing deeper cooperation in advance of the visit of the Dutch Minister for Foreign Trade to Saudi Arabia in December 2025, which will include a business delegation focused on hydrogen and critical raw materials.RemarkDue to the transparency with regard to the IATI projects, a non-ODA country has been included in this project.</narrative>
  </description>
